# Smoke test for #88 (mesh angvel). Load in the Map Viewer / a real match and
# confirm both blades visibly spin: TopLevelSpin orbits world origin (upstream's
# own behaviour for a hand-authored spin with no enclosing group), while the two
# GroupBlade instances each spin in place about their own placed position.
#
# Every blade is written as two faces over the same corners in opposite order,
# which is how a BZW map asks for a two-sided surface -- a spinning blade that
# vanished for half of each turn would make the test harder to read, not
# easier. See docs/bzw.md, "Two-sided surfaces".

# Sized to the blades and nothing else. TopLevelSpin's own orbit reaches 35
# units from the origin and the two GroupBlade instances reach 35 along each
# axis, so walls at 50 leave a margin to stand in without the eye having to
# cross a quarter of a kilometre of empty ground to see what is being tested.
world
	size 50
end

material
	name spinmat
	diffuse 1 0 0 1
end

mesh
	name TopLevelSpin
	angvel 90
	vertex 25 0 0
	vertex 35 0 0
	vertex 30 0 5
	face
		vertices 0 1 2
		matref spinmat
		passable
	endface
	face #backside
		vertices 0 2 1
		matref spinmat
		passable
	endface
end

define SpinBlade
	mesh
		angvel 45
		vertex -5 0 0
		vertex 5 0 0
		vertex 0 0 8
		face
			vertices 0 1 2
			matref spinmat
			passable
		endface
		face #backside
			vertices 0 2 1
			matref spinmat
			passable
		endface
	end
enddef

group SpinBlade
	shift -30 -30 0
end

group SpinBlade
	shift 30 30 0
end
